WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.436
-My first guest is
an Oscar-winning icon

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:06.038
who is now guest-starring in
the fourth season of

00:00:06.038 --> 00:00:07.407
"Search Party" on HBO Max.

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:09.375
The final four episodes
of Season 4

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:11.344
begin streaming this Thursday.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:13.746
Here she is, Susan Sarandon.

00:00:13.746 --> 00:00:17.450
Oh! This is --
Susan, I -- I'm honored.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.618
-Welcome.

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:20.520
-I'm so honored to be
welcomed into your home.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.688
This is amazing.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:24.023
-Yes, I have not let anyone
film in my house,

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:26.526
even Barbara Walters,
when she wanted to.

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.228
Oprah, no.
-Yeah.

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:30.529
-And now here you are.
-Unbelievable.

00:00:30.529 --> 00:00:33.399
-You're a little, tiny piece
of my New York apartment.

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:35.000
-Oh, I'm so happy.
-Yeah.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.503
-Yeah, we just started --
Well, we came back

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:40.973
to the studio to do these shows
here with, like,

00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:42.542
remote cameras
and stuff like that,

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:43.876
and so there's no family here.

00:00:43.876 --> 00:00:46.679
There's no kids running around.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:48.047
-Yeah, they've been
torturing you.

00:00:48.047 --> 00:00:51.050
I think people have developed
such an appreciation of

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:55.288
teachers and moms
that work at home

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:57.723
and without alcohol or drugs.

00:00:57.723 --> 00:01:00.125
It's a big deal. Yeah.

00:01:00.125 --> 00:01:02.995
-It really, really is.

00:01:02.995 --> 00:01:05.498
Franny just lost her
second tooth yesterday,

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:06.832
right here.

00:01:06.832 --> 00:01:09.169
-Did they come out naturally
or did you take it out?

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:12.238
-She pulled it out.
It came out naturally.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:15.741
-My granddaughter --
My eldest granddaughter's father

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:19.279
is an ex-soccer pro,
Kyle Martino.

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:22.482
So, her tooth was wiggling,
and she was at his house

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:23.716
in Brooklyn.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:28.988
And he taped a string
to a soccer ball.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:32.892
He taped floss to a soccer ball,
put it around her tooth,

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:35.528
and kicked it.

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:39.431
And it worked, but then guess
what the downside of that is.

00:01:39.431 --> 00:01:42.335
Where's the tooth?
-Yeah, the tooth is gone.

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:43.736
-Yeah, you can't find the tooth.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:46.472
So, the second one,
they did a better job,

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:49.375
and she kicked
the ball herself,

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.778
and they managed to
keep an eye on the tooth.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:54.547
But it started
a whole tradition.

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:58.418
that I think only
a soccer pro -- footballer --

00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:59.885
would think to do.

00:01:59.885 --> 00:02:02.988
-I'm always happy to see you,
and I actually have been

00:02:02.988 --> 00:02:05.158
seeing you recently
pop up online

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:06.826
with these paparazzi shots.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:08.094
I don't know if you know what
I'm talking about.

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:11.130
You're walking -- You take walks
with Jessica Lange,

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.399
apparently,
around New York City.

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:14.700
Oh, there it is.
We have a photo.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.302
That's you and Jessica Lange.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:19.505
And then there's photos of you,
like, helping people,

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:22.542
like, helping people
cross the street

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:24.677
and all these nice,
Good Samaritan things.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:25.845
And people are saying online

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:29.248
that they think that
you guys are superheroes.

00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:30.249
-We are.

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:32.251
But, you know,
look at what it --

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:34.754
Look at what that tells you
about the paparazzi.

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:37.023
How desperate are they that
they're following

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:40.292
two bundled-up people -- you
can't even tell who we are --

00:02:40.292 --> 00:02:42.629
for an hour and a half in
Lower Manhattan,

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:44.363
just hoping something's
going to happen?

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:47.366
And, so, Jess and I were saying,
"Maybe this time when we go out,

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:49.435
we're going to have to
find, like, a burning building

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:51.170
or someone down a manhole."

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:54.374
-Yeah. I'll stage something
with you guys if you want me to.

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:57.209
-Yeah. I know.
That was really -- That's a lot.

00:02:57.209 --> 00:02:58.278
That's a lot.

00:02:58.278 --> 00:03:00.113
-Oh, you know what
I want to ask you?

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:03.482
Because everyone's at home,
and they're watching

00:03:03.482 --> 00:03:05.351
all these movies
and their favorite movies.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:09.154
And "Thelma &amp; Louise"
has had a total resurgence.

00:03:09.154 --> 00:03:11.624
Everyone's like --
New generations are watching it,

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:12.925
talking about it.

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:14.159
-Oh, good.
-Yeah.

00:03:14.159 --> 00:03:15.962
People dressing up as you guys.

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:18.464
-I didn't know that.
That's cool.

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:21.333
-Obviously, the ending of the
film -- I can't spoil it now --

00:03:21.333 --> 00:03:25.305
but when you -- Did you ever go
to Grand Canyon at all?

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:27.606
And if you ever do,
do people go, like --

00:03:27.606 --> 00:03:29.708
Do they get excited or do they
go, "How'd you get here?"

00:03:29.708 --> 00:03:33.913
-Years ago,
I did have a really great --

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.781
Well, someone had
a really great moment,

00:03:35.781 --> 00:03:37.717
because I was with
my youngest son.

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:40.285
We were doing a trip around
and we were in

00:03:40.285 --> 00:03:41.620
the Grand Canyon briefly.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:44.190
And we went into the gift shop,
and there were two women

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.825
who were doing a
"Thelma &amp; Louise" trip.

00:03:46.825 --> 00:03:49.295
And there I was welcoming them,

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:54.133
making an extra 25 cents
to push my movie.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.502
-See? Yeah,
that's how hard you work.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:59.372
-They talked about a sequel,
but I could not --

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:02.074
I don't know what it would be.

00:04:02.074 --> 00:04:03.609
I can't understand.

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:05.077
-No, it would be like --

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:06.779
Do you remember the movie --
Was it "Topper"?

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:08.981
Do you remember that movie?
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:08.981 --> 00:04:11.251
Actually, that was
a very bad idea they had,

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:14.520
of we were ghosts
looking down on Earth

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:20.593
and helping women who were in
domestic -- bad dome-- Yeah.

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:21.961
And I said --
I remember saying to Tim,

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.162
"But what would we be doing?"

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:25.531
And he said,
"You'd be getting a big check."

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:29.167
-[ Laughs ]
That's a good line, at least.

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:31.437
-No, that didn't work out.
-No, that didn't work out.

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:32.838
-Best to leave it alone.

00:04:32.838 --> 00:04:35.908
-Oh, you know, I heard a fun
story about you and Geena Davis.

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:39.278
Is this true that, one time,
she dressed up as a bear

00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:43.082
and, like, scared your kids
at a camp-out?

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:46.819
-We were having --
I was throwing my daughter

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:49.422
a camping party
in our living room,

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:53.392
and so they were going to do
hot dogs on the fire

00:04:53.392 --> 00:04:57.730
and they were -- I got,
you know, cassettes of

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:58.931
animal noises.

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:01.133
And they were sleeping
right in the living room.

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:03.936
And we had the bear suit,
of course.

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:05.637
We provided the bear suit.

00:05:05.637 --> 00:05:09.275
But Geena, very nicely,
did a very good job of

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:10.409
wearing that bear suit.

00:05:10.409 --> 00:05:12.578
And she did briefly,
but she's not --

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:14.847
You know, for somebody
who is formidable,

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:17.182
she's not very scary, actually.

00:05:17.182 --> 00:05:19.819
-She's not, but, yeah,
in a bear suit, though.

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:24.023
-She couldn't really -- She just
revealed herself way soon.

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:25.891
-And just started laughing.

00:05:25.891 --> 00:05:28.127
I want to talk to you about
"Search Party."

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:30.262
What can we say
about "Search party"? And --

00:05:30.262 --> 00:05:36.168
-So many funny things.
So out of the box.

00:05:36.168 --> 00:05:40.173
So -- All of these kids that
are in it are so good.

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:42.374
I'm kind of playing
the plot twist,

00:05:42.374 --> 00:05:46.611
so you'll see -- You didn't
even see where it goes.

00:05:46.611 --> 00:05:47.880
And I had so much fun.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.915
And you can
tell, when you watch it,

00:05:49.915 --> 00:05:52.584
that everybody that's on it
is having so much fun.

00:05:52.584 --> 00:05:54.220
But, at the same time,
Cole Escola

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:59.258
makes an appearance now
in a big part in this season,

00:05:59.258 --> 00:06:00.960
and they get really scary.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.395
-It's brilliant.

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:04.997
-Well, it was a job that,
actually, my son got me.

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:06.832
It's nepotism,
because he knows Charles,

00:06:06.832 --> 00:06:09.268
and so he said, "Mom,
I think they're interested,

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:11.570
and would you like to?"

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:14.073
And so I really --
Now I start getting jobs

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:15.508
because of my children.

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:16.876
-See? It comes full circle.

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:19.544
-And, also, "Motherlover"
was like that,

00:06:19.544 --> 00:06:22.148
because my youngest was like,
"Mom, you have to do it."

00:06:22.148 --> 00:06:25.684
I didn't know what
"Dick in a Box" was.

00:06:25.684 --> 00:06:27.319
And he was like,
"It's a classic.

00:06:27.319 --> 00:06:29.288
Whatever they ask you to do,
you have to do it.

00:06:29.288 --> 00:06:31.390
Absolutely."
So I did it.

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:32.791
-That ends up happening, right?

00:06:32.791 --> 00:06:36.261
Your kids end up going like,
"No, mom, dad, this is cool.

00:06:36.261 --> 00:06:38.296
That's not cool. Do this thing."
-Yeah.

00:06:38.296 --> 00:06:39.498
-And you're like, "Okay."

00:06:39.498 --> 00:06:41.467
Yeah, already,
I'm trying to please my kids,

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:43.469
and that's why
I'm not going to host

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:44.469
"The Tonight Show" anymore.

00:06:44.469 --> 00:06:48.540
I'm the now voice of Peppa Pig.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:51.944
-It will pay off later.
It will pay off later.

00:06:51.944 --> 00:06:53.145
Right now, not so much.

00:06:53.145 --> 00:06:55.014
Right now,
you're in the trenches.

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:57.450
But it eventually --
It pays off.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.885
-Alright, good.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:59.885 --> 00:07:02.888
Here's Susan Sarandon in
Season 4 of "Search Party."

00:07:02.888 --> 00:07:04.723
Take a look at this.

00:07:04.723 --> 00:07:05.958
-Call baby brother.

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:07.125
[ Ringtone ]

00:07:07.125 --> 00:07:08.327
-Hello?
-Richard.

00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:10.963
I made it to Babyfoot
and I'm in the house.

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:13.399
Uh, chip is not.

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:15.767
The situation
has turned sour, though.

00:07:15.767 --> 00:07:18.403
Uh, there's a dead body.
-Oh. The Dory girl?

00:07:18.403 --> 00:07:20.840
-Oh. Uh...

00:07:22.441 --> 00:07:26.278
No, I don't think
it is the Dory girl.

00:07:26.278 --> 00:07:29.649
This woman is old.

00:07:29.649 --> 00:07:30.916
Provincial.

00:07:30.916 --> 00:07:35.421
Oh, and there's
a room full of chains.

00:07:35.421 --> 00:07:39.759
Uh, I don't remember them being
there when we bought the house.

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:40.826
-Susan Sarandon.

00:07:40.826 --> 00:07:42.594
Check out
the final four episodes of

00:07:42.594 --> 00:07:46.899
Season 4 of "Search Party" this
Thursday on HBO Max.

